>>
endobj
108 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 55 0 R
/E (Doctors Without Borders is committed to providing emergency medical aid to people in crisis. To this end, it runs humanitarian projects in more than 70 countries, often performing its work under difficult circumstances in crisis-affected and vulnerable areas. In such circumstances, reliable and fast on-premises access to relevant information is crucial.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
109 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 55 0 R
/E (This challenge tasks participants with designing a document retrieval tool to support doctors operating in crisis-affected and vulnerable areas in reliably and quickly identifying relevant documents. Ideally, this tool can be fully run on-premises \(that is, on location\), successfully identifies relevant documents, returns a minimal number of false positives, is cost-efficient, and does not create dependency on a specific vendor. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
110 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 55 0 R
/T (Challenge goal)
/E (Challenge goal)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
111 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 55 0 R
/E (Doctors Without Borders has provided a collection of free-text documents from practice, with topics ranging from medicine to administrative affairs, and with locations spread out over different continents. The goal is to design a document retrieval tool that identifies relevant documents when provided with a textual query. The document retrieval step may, but does not need to be, supported by a document preprocessing step. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
112 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 55 0 R
/E (An ideal tool would be:)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
