<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 381 0 R
/E (Effective: It would reliably and quickly identify relevant documents.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
114 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 382 0 R
/E (Cost-effective: Its cost-per-query, implementation cost and maintenance cost would be limited.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
115 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 383 0 R
/E (Maintainable: Its design and dependencies would be amenable to updates and changing requirements from the field.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
116 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 384 0 R
/E (Usable on-premises: It would be usable in locations with poor internet connection, limited computer storage capacity, and limited computing power. Note that document preprocessing does not need to be performed on-premises.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
