130 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 56 0 R
/E (Doctors Without Borders \(DWB\) is an international humanitarian medical organization that provides medical care to those affected by war, epidemics, natural disasters, and extreme poverty. Its work is based on medical need, regardless of nationality, religion, political views, or background. Doctors and nurses work alongside psychologists, logisticians, data scientists, and other specialists. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
131 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 56 0 R
/E (DWB was founded in France in 1971 by doctors and journalists who had witnessed the devastating Biafran War and famine in Nigeria. They wanted to create an organization that could respond quickly to humanitarian crises and speak openly about what its teams encountered. From the beginning, DWB has been guided by three principles: impartiality, neutrality, and independence. These mean providing assistance according to need, avoiding political sides, and remaining free from outside interests.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
132 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 56 0 R
/E (In the past decades, DWB has grown into a worldwide humanitarian movement with over 65,000 people. Its teams have responded to conflicts, refugee crises, epidemics, natural disasters, and disease outbreaks, while also working on issues such as malnutrition, maternal healthcare, vaccination, and mental health. In 1999, DWB received the Nobel Peace Prize for its humanitarian work. Today, its teams operate in more than 70 countries, often in crisis-affected and vulnerable areas. Its core principles remain providing medical care to people who need it most while maintaining the independence to act and speak freely.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
